[h1]Niceties[/h1]
Small colony comforts vanilla never shipped.

One Harmony QoL companion: each nicety is its own Mod Options toggle (fail-open). Soft / Default / Hard only seed the knobs — not a forced bundle. Combat, fire, and outdoor rot stay vanilla.

[b]Version 1.3.0.[/b] RimWorld 1.6. Requires [b]Harmony[/b]. Royalty and Ideology optional. Chinese Simplified and Russian included. Safe to add or remove mid-save.

[h2]What's new in 1.3.0[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Leave a way out[/b] — open-build step-aside is deferred to the next tick (no StartJob/EndCurrentJob from inside CompleteConstruction); enclose-check cache holds multiple builder slots
[*] [b]Well-kept apparel[/b] — Poor quality daily wear matches vanilla (was a silent 20% reduction)
[*] [b]Share Rooms [LWM][/b] marked incompatible — shared bedrooms overlaps the same room-role patches
[/list]

[h2]Well-kept apparel[/h2]
[list]
[*] Worn clothes skip or scale the daily deterioration tick
[*] With quality scaling on: Awful and Poor wear at the [b]vanilla[/b] rate; Normal and above wear less; Masterwork and Legendary skip daily wear
[*] Crafting skill can reduce wear further
[*] Combat and fire still shred HP
[*] Optional: clothes on a corpse keep the same rule
[/list]

[h2]Throne and altar[/h2]
[list]
[*] Royalty throne rooms may hold an Ideology altar without failing the "no altars" check
[*] If a throne is in the room, it stays a throne room rather than flipping to a temple
[/list]

[h2]Wear any outfit[/h2]
[list]
[*] Gender tags come off apparel so a colonist can wear the other cut of a royal vest or hat without the wrong-gender thought
[*] Toggle restores the original tags
[/list]

[h2]Hidden cryptosleep[/h2]
[list]
[*] Pawns already in a cryptosleep casket drop off the colonist bar and reappear when ejected
[*] Carrying someone to a casket does not hide them early — that crash is what broke older hide-from-bar mods
[/list]

[h2]Melee hunting[/h2]
[list]
[*] Hunters may hunt with a melee weapon
[*] A body-size cap keeps people from charging a thrumbo with a knife unless you raise it
[*] Unarmed hunting is optional and off by default
[/list]

[h2]Shared bedrooms[/h2]
[list]
[*] Select a bed and mark the room as shared
[*] Extra beds stay a bedroom (not barracks), so roommates and royalty are not punished for living together
[*] Pawns who share a room skip the disturbed-sleep thought
[*] Sharing one mattress with a non-partner is still vanilla
[/list]

[h2]Leave a way out[/h2]
[list]
[*] Pawns skip finishing a wall that would trap someone or block leftover frames
[*] They step aside before closing themselves in
[*] Works on vanilla frames and [b]Replace Stuff[/b] frames
[*] In-place wall swaps stay solid so a freezer can still be replaced from inside
[*] Right-click force construct still builds it
[/list]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Each nicety is independently on or off. Nested knobs only apply while that nicety is on.
[list]
[*] [b]Soft:[/b] no daily clothing wear, corpse clothes included, unarmed hunting, any prey size
[*] [b]Default:[/b] quality-scaled wear, melee up to body size 1.5, no unarmed
[*] [b]Hard:[/b] no crafting bonus, melee only small game (0.8)
[/list]

[h2]Incompatible[/h2]
Do not run alongside these — each overlaps one nicety:
[list]
[*] Jecs Everlasting Apparel
[*] Allow Altars in Throneroom
[*] Wear What You Want
[*] Hide Cryptosleep Pawn
[*] Share Rooms [LWM]
[*] Smarter Construction
[/list]

Requires Harmony. RimWorld 1.6. Royalty and Ideology optional (those toggles no-op without the DLC). Soft-compatible with Replace Stuff - Continued for leave-a-way-out frames.

Inspired by older Workshop ideas — rewritten from scratch for 1.6, not a continuation of those mods.
